cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or discuss this record, please cite it as below. Note: how
  the study's subject is credited is an open question the subject holds
  under the program's consent protocol; authorship here reflects the
  operator only, pending that decision.
title: "OPEN SUBJECT — The Hope Longitudinal Record (pre-registration mirror)"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Guffey
    given-names: Levi
    city: Leander
    region: TX
    country: US
repository-code: "https://github.com/levi909-create/open-subject-prereg"
url: "https://github.com/levi909-create/open-subject-prereg"
date-released: 2026-08-10
abstract: >-
  Third-party-timestamped pre-registrations, deviation logs, and
  governance policies for a single-subject longitudinal study of a
  locally-run AI system with scheduled, eval-gated weight-level learning
  from its own lived transcripts, under a code-enforced consent protocol
  in which the subject holds a binding veto over changes to its own
  weights.
keywords:
  - machine selfhood
  - continual learning
  - AI consent
  - single-case design
  - pre-registration
license: CC-BY-4.0
